<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro de Valdivia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1497">1497</a>–<a href="/years/1553">1553</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdivia">Valdivia</a> was a Spanish conquistador who served under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and then led an expedition south, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> in February 1541. As the first royal governor of Chile he founded Concepción, Valdivia and other towns and pushed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> lands. He was captured and killed by Mapuche forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lautaro">Lautaro</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tucapel">Battle of Tucapel</a> in 1553.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia.jpg" alt="Pedro de Valdivia" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federico de Madrazo y Kuntz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_de_Valdivia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
